{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

{% include "header.njk" %}

<div class="pg-page">
  <header class="pg-hero">
    <p class="section-label">Playground</p>
    <h1>Things built for the fun of it</h1>
    <p class="pg-lede">Not products, not on a roadmap. These exist because a problem looked interesting. Some are browser-only; features that make network requests say so.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="pg-feature" aria-labelledby="console-title">
    <div class="pg-feature-body">
      <p class="section-label">Site console</p>
      <h2 id="console-title">Navigate the site from a command palette</h2>
      <p>Press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>`</kbd> (or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>`</kbd>) anywhere on this site to open a keyboard command palette. It searches all {{ stats.liveTools }} utilities by name and keyword, navigates between projects and docs, jumps to recorded demos, and launches the experiments below.</p>
      <p>It reads the same machine-readable tool index that AI agents consume at <a href="/tools/index.json">/tools/index.json</a>, so its catalog is generated from the site's current tool data. Tab completes, <kbd>↑</kbd> walks history, <kbd>Esc</kbd> closes.</p>
      <button type="button" class="pg-btn" data-open-console>{{ icon("terminal", 16) }} <span>Open the console</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-feature-demo" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="pg-mock">
        <div class="pg-mock-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>penumbraforge — console</em></div>
        <pre class="pg-mock-body"><span class="pg-p">/ $</span> find jwt
<span class="pg-k">jwt-decoder</span>   Decode and inspect JSON Web Token headers.
<span class="pg-k">jwt-attack</span>    Test tokens against real attack classes.
<span class="pg-d">2 shown. "open &lt;slug&gt;" to launch.</span>

<span class="pg-p">/ $</span> cd gate
<span class="pg-d">now at /gate/</span>

<span class="pg-p">/gate/ $</span> demo gate
<span class="pg-d">→ /gate/#demo</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="experiments-title">
    <p class="section-label">Experiments</p>
    <h2 id="experiments-title" class="pg-h2">Three that escaped</h2>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <a class="pg-card" href="/terminal/">
        <span class="pg-card-ic">{{ icon("terminal") }}</span>
        <h3>Browser terminal</h3>
        <p>A terminal emulator that runs in a tab and generates <code>curl</code>, Fetch, and Axios request snippets; it does not execute those network requests. It started as a way to explore the tools without leaving the page.</p>
        <span class="pg-card-go">Open terminal <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      </a>
      <a class="pg-card" href="/game/">
        <span class="pg-card-ic">{{ icon("shield") }}</span>
        <h3>BREACH</h3>
        <p>A roguelike where you work through a compromised network. The security concepts are real even though the network isn't — reconnaissance, lateral movement, and the part where you get caught.</p>
        <span class="pg-card-go">Play BREACH <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      </a>
      <a class="pg-card" href="/snake/">
        <span class="pg-card-ic">{{ icon("chip") }}</span>
        <h3>Snake</h3>
        <p>Snake. In the eclipse palette. There is no deeper justification and there does not need to be one.</p>
        <span class="pg-card-go">Play snake <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-foot">All three are reachable from the console too — type <code>terminal</code>, <code>breach</code>, or <code>snake</code>.</p>
  </section>
</div>

